🔹 REST API Design
1. What is the key principle you follow when designing a RESTful API?
answer:
    1. Use Nouns in URLs (Resource-Oriented)
        ✅ Good: GET /orders/123
        ❌ Bad: GET /getOrderDetails?id=123
        This makes APIs predictable and aligns with REST semantics.
    2. Use HTTP Methods Properly
    3. Status Codes Must Reflect Response
        ✅ 200 OK, 201 Created, 204 No Content
        ❌ Avoid always returning 200 with error in body
        Used @ControllerAdvice for global exception handling
        example:
        @ExceptionHandler(EntityNotFoundException.class)
        public ResponseEntity<String> handleNotFound() {
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body("Entity not found");
        }
    4. Pagination & Filtering
        ✅ GET /products?page=1&size=10&category=electronics
        Implemented with Pageable in Spring Boot:
        public Page<Product> getProducts(Pageable pageable) { ... }
    5. Use DTOs Instead of Entities
    6. Version Your APIs


