🔹 Kafka & Microservices
1. How do you containerize a Spring Boot application using Docker? What steps and considerations are involved?
answer:
    1. Build Your Spring Boot JAR: ./mvnw clean package --> This creates a target/myapp.jar
    2. Create a Dockerfile in Project Root
    3. Build the Docker Image: docker build -t my-spring-boot-app .--> This creates a local image called my-spring-boot-app.
    4. Run the Docker Container: docker run -p 8080:8080 my-spring-boot-app

    | Step              | Command / File                                     |
    | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
    | Build JAR         | `./mvnw clean package`                             |
    | Create Dockerfile | Use `FROM openjdk`, `COPY`, `EXPOSE`, `ENTRYPOINT` |
    | Build Image       | `docker build -t my-spring-boot-app .`             |
    | Run Container     | `docker run -p 8080:8080 my-spring-boot-app`       |


